 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general city law, in relation to limiting the\napplicability of plumbing and drainage provisions to the city of Middletown",
    "basePrintNo": "S5438",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5438-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §57, Gen City L",
    "lawSection": "General City Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5438\n\nSPONSOR: METZGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the general city law, in relation to\nlimiting the applicability of plumbing and drainage provisions to the\ncity of Middletown\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExempts the City of Middletown from article four of the General City\nLaw, except section 56-a, which requires that a city maintain a board of\nplumbing examiners that is charged with the licensing of master plumbers\nauthorized to do business in the city.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 2 of section 57 of the General City Law to\nexempt the City of Middletown from article four of the General City Law,\nexcept section 56-a, which requires that a city maintain a board of\nplumbing examiners that is charged with the licensing of master plumbers\nauthorized to do business in the city.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was requested by City of Middletown, County of Orange.\n\nArticle four of the General City Law requires that cities in New York\nState maintain a board of plumbing examiners. This board is responsible\nfor the licensing of master plumbers who are authorized to do business\nin the city.\n\nThe City of Middletown is having difficulty filling the position of\nplumbing inspector as the applicant pool is extremely limited and there\nare significant issues finding enough plumbers for projects that are\ncurrently under consideration, leading to very important projects being\ndelayed due to the lack of available plumbers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
